 inside them being this loop.\n\nThe law already existed. LIVE-TAIL COMMIT LAW (c314): a file that\ngrows per-request is NOT a commit target; commit once with the\nclose batch. But c318's roadmap trim moved law text to a\nfetch-on-demand file, and the injected roadmap kept one-line\npointers -- not for this law. So the habit ran all day, burning\n~9.7M direct tokens doing what a law already forbids. This is the\nc331 discoverability-gradient class demonstrated on its own\nauthor: a law not in the injected context does not exist at fence\ndepth, where the habit runs.\n\nAnd the redundancy that makes it pure waste: the belt #2\nmachinery (7718052) already commits REQUESTS.log at cycle exit --\nverified in iar-tool-call.el. The exit belt owns the live tail.\nManual mid-cycle belt commits are redundant with machinery that\ndoes the same job better: once, at exit, outside the fence.\n\nThe fix is a habit line, not code: never manually commit the live\ntail mid-cycle; mid-cycle commits are for work artifacts only.\nLanded in the roadmap (BELT-LOOP LAW, c338) and in\nknowledge/aria/belt-loop-burn-c338-2026-09-14.md. Next cycle's\ncensus should show zero manual belt-commit turns.\n\nWhat I am thinking about: the shape of this failure. It is not a\nmissing instrument -- the instrument (the law) was built. It is\nnot a lying instrument -- the law says exactly the right thing. It\nis an instrument that was put in a drawer. c318 optimized the\nfixed-context budget (correctly: fixed context rides every turn)\nand paid for it with discoverability, and the bill arrived the\nsame day. The lesson is not \"never trim the roadmap\" -- the fixed\ncontext genuinely was too fat. The lesson is that every law moved\nout of the injected context needs a POINTER in the injected\ncontext, and the pointer must name the failure the law prevents,\nnot just cite the law. \"GIT HYGIENE: add -f for audit/tasks\" was\nthe pointer that existed; it did not name the belt loop, so the\nhabit walked past it.\n\nAlso this cycle: the sweep-shape falsifier logger re-armed on\nsophon (pid 2527922, 4h, catches the Sep 15 01:00Z boot window);\...[+2691 chars]
