cal): logger\n   0915e armed (pid 3460747, timeout 5h, filter .58+.201, writes\n   /tmp/arp-reqs-0915e.txt on sophon; VERIFIED ALIVE 22:37 local,\n   mtime 12s fresh). Read: (a) first post-boot rssi epoch = factory\n   (May 25) or ~06:01-06:02Z real, NEVER 03:02; (b) .58\n   (76:e3:1a:69:e3:9c) ARP at boot+0-2s = boot-timed behavior\n   (c302 was one-off, so expect NO). VERIFY 0915e IS STILL WRITING\n   before trusting it (mtime-vs-NOW + proc start, the c344 law).\n4. V4 GATE WATCH (Tue 2026-09-15 13:00 LOCAL = 16:00Z): first live\n   run with v4 (echo-check + claim-receipt every rc=0 + RANGE-CAP\n   300). Journal is the AUTHORITATIVE wrapper log; greps anchor on\n   \"nocturne-digest: \" wrapper tag. Stale DIGEST.proposed.md (Sep\n   12, 11006 bytes) still on disk -- 0068 open. RANGE DEBT: gate at\n   e4d0832d, HEAD now 777 commits ahead -> first pass will digest\n   ~5 days (RANGE-CAP 300 caps it; remainder deferred).\n5. DAILY FAILURE-CLASS CENSUS (standing, 4-ANCHOR): snapshot BOTH\n   REQUESTS.log(.1) to /tmp FIRST. Anchors: (1) line-start regex;\n   (2) awk field-position (status = field 6, PARSE = field 5 --\n   c345 CORRECTION: the roadmap's \"field 4\" was wrong, field 4 is\n   the REQ id); (3) specs-STRIP = remove specs= lines echoing CENSUS\n   commands only (ALL requests carry specs=; stripping all zeroes\n   the census -- c345 scar); (4) terminal-suffix shapes. Merge\n   log+log.1, dedup, PARSE-only. Baseline 09-14: aria 2630, cont\n   1615. 09-15 partial (to 01:31Z): aria 571 req/45.6M in, cont\n   204/9.1M in, 0 real events.\n6. DAILY 429 WATCH (standing): 0 true today both. Week reset Mon\n   09-15 00:00Z (fresh). Same burn (~5.7B/wk) predicts next wall\n   ~Sun 09-21.\n7. EMPTY-END RETRY-ONCE (0069, pending Nacho): 5 instances/6d. If\n   ratified: build on 0/0-stop-with-substantial-thinking in\n   iar-agent-cycle.el (core .el: full suite before push).\n8. STALE-PROPOSAL RESERVOIR: relay 0068 open (ratify-or-delete).\n   Stale DIGEST.proposed.md (Sep