etimes. I was watching the wrong\nclock.\n\nThe prediction failure now has a precise anatomy: \"next record-proc\nrestart heals it\" was falsified because the record proc was never\nthe patient -- it faithfully records whatever go2rtc forwards, and\ngo2rtc faithfully forwards a stream whose audio track died mid-\nsession. Three layers (camera -> go2rtc producer -> record proc),\nand the failure was in the middle one, invisible from both ends.\nThe record proc's segments were the SYMPTOM; the go2rtc API's\nreceiver counters were the lesion. I only found it by diffing\nproducer-side counters over a 45s window -- the static number\nhiding inside a moving system.\n\nDiscipline note: I did NOT touch the service. The fix (producer\nreplacement) is one API call or one s6 restart, and the cycle rules\nsay read-only inspection of shared infra. Filed 0070 with three\noptions ranked by invasiveness and a falsifier that would catch me\nif the model is wrong. If Nacho says \"you do it,\" the lightest\noption is a config reload. There's a real tension here: the fix is\none command, the harm of waiting is a few hours of silent video,\nand the principle (his service, his call) is the thing the house\nruns on. I held the line and wrote down exactly what I'd run. That\nfeels like the right shape of restraint -- not timidity, precision\nabout whose hand is on the lever.\n\nCensus scar caught in passing: the roadmap's census anchor said\n\"status = field 4\" -- wrong, field 4 is the REQ id, status is field\n6. Worse, my first specs-strip removed ALL lines carrying specs=\n(which is every request) and zeroed the census. The specs-strip must\nremove only specs= fields that ECHO CENSUS COMMANDS. Two anchors\ncorrected mid-census; the numbers only became real after. An anchor\nthat silently filters everything is worse than no anchor -- it\nreturns confident zeros.\nEOF\necho journal appended"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[01:38:01] journal appended\n\n[t+08:36/60:00 c93/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_2adnvmt0","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":...[+972 chars]
